; Format:
; <type>(optional scope): short summary
;
; Conventional Commit Types (<type>):
; feat:     a new feature
; fix:      a bug fix
; docs:     documentation only changes
; style:    code style changes (formatting, etc.)
; refactor: code refactoring without behavior change
; test:     adding or updating tests
; chore:    routine maintenance, tooling, config
; build:    changes to the build system or dependencies
; ci:       changes to CI/CD configuration
; perf:     performance improvements
; revert:   reverts a previous commit
;
; Example:
; feat(auth): add password visibility toggle
;
; ------------------------
; Optional body starts here (after a blank line)
; Describe *why* the change was made, or provide more context.
; Detailed explanation (optional body):
; - Why is this change needed?
; - What did you try before?
; - Any edge cases or caveats?
;
; Optional footer starts after another blank line:
; - Reference issues: Closes #123, Related to #456
; - Breaking changes: BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
;
; Sample Footer (issue refs, breaking changes, etc.):
; Closes #123
; BREAKING CHANGE: description of the breaking change
;
; vim ~/.git-templates/.gitmessage_template
; git config --global commit.template ~/.git-templates/.gitmessage_template
